# EOY agent router

Before planning or coding in this repo:

1. Skim [docs/INDEX.md](../../docs/INDEX.md) for the right canon doc.
2. Treat [DESIGN.md](../../DESIGN.md) § Design locks as product law. Do not “fix” intentional asymmetry (R1, A13/F1, F5–F7, A14, R2) without an explicit design-lock change.
3. Prefer project skills under `.cursor/skills/` for procedures; prefer project agents under `.cursor/agents/` for role handoffs.
4. Before claiming done on sim, placement, routing, or Rust changes: follow `eoy-qa-lifecycle` (and rebuild DLL via `eoy-rust-gdextension` if `rust/empire_territory/src/` changed).

## Skill map

| Situation | Skill |
|-----------|--------|
| Multi-agent feature / review loop | `eoy-multi-agent-handoff` |
| Headless QA / smoke / Godot path | `eoy-qa-lifecycle` |
| Rust crate / GDExtension / DLL | `eoy-rust-gdextension` |
| Live paint, domain pulls, WorldDataset | `eoy-scd1-presentation` |
| Changing a design lock | `eoy-design-lock-change` |
| Menu / HUD / GameTheme / globe chrome | `eoy-ui-theme` |

## Agent map

| Role | Agent |
|------|--------|
| Vision, stories, acceptance, final QA | `product-manager` |
| Full-stack implement plan / code | `coding-architect` |
| Bugs, dead code, evidence | `exterminator` |
| SCD1 / WorldDataset / sim data truth | `data-architect` |
| Look/feel, layouts, theme QA | `ui-ux-designer` |

Canonical product truth stays in markdown docs — skills link to docs; do not duplicate DESIGN.md into prompts.
